            {
              "box": 510
            },
            {
              "box": 515
            },
            {
              "box": 525
            },
            {
              "box": 528
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Tax reconciliation",
          "rows": [
            {
              "box": 595,
              "note": "The sheet leaves this an input. Enter what you have already paid."
            },
            {
              "box": 600
            },
            {
              "box": 605,
              "rule": {
                "op": "positiveDifference",
                "cells": ["Financialaccounts.xlsx!CT600!AJ163", "Financialaccounts.xlsx!CT600!AJ159"],
                "why": "the sheet's own overpaid cell AJ169 is not a read; box 605 is tax already paid less the self-assessment, floored at nil"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Indicators and information",
          "rows": [
            {
              "box": 620
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Capital allowances and balancing charges",
          "rows": [
            {
              "box": 690,
              "cell": "Financialaccounts.xlsx!CorporationTax!I15"
            },
            {
              "box": 695,
              "empty": true,
              "note": "The working sheet has no special rate pool."
            },
            {
              "box": 700,
              "empty": true,
              "note": "The working sheet has no special rate pool."
            },
            {
              "box": 705,
              "rule": {
                "op": "sum",
                "cells": [
                  "Financialaccounts.xlsx!CorporationTax!I16",
                  "Financialaccounts.xlsx!CorporationTax!I17",
                  "positivePartOf(Financialaccounts.xlsx!CorporationTax!I18)"
                ],
                "why": "Version 3 has one main pool box, so the cars line, the assets-held line and any balancing allowance join it; the CT600 sheet's own AA177 and AA179 read column H of the working sheet, which is empty on rows 15 to 18, so they print blank on every package"
              },
              "note": "The CT600 sheet leaves this box blank. The figure comes from the corporation tax working sheet."
            },
            {
              "box": 710,
              "rule": {
                "op": "sum",
                "cells": ["negativePartOf(Financialaccounts.xlsx!CorporationTax!I18)"],
                "why": "the working sheet carries a balancing charge as a negative allowance, so only the part of that line below nil is a charge; the sheet's own AL177 reads column H, which is empty"
              },
              "note": "The CT600 sheet leaves this box blank. The figure comes from the corporation tax working sheet."
            },
            {
              "box": 760,
              "empty": true,
              "note": "The working sheet claims the annual investment allowance, not a first year allowance."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Declaration",
          "rows": [
            {
              "box": 975,
              "cell": "Financialaccounts.xlsx!OpenAccounts!E5"
            },
            {
              "box": 980,
              "empty": true,
              "note": "Enter the date you sign the return."
